[Section: 16. Source tree / software architecture]

The application is extremely compact:

Inside `Vehicle.c`, behavior is organized around:

- a struct representing current vehicle/control state;

- menu-driven input;

- helper functions that mutate state through pointers;

- branch logic mapping simulated sensor values to outputs;

- repeated status printing.

This is a **single-process procedural architecture** with mutable state passed into helper functions.

[Section: 16. Source tree / software architecture > Architectural strengths]

- explicit state container rather than scattering every value independently;

- helper functions separate some control concerns;

- input → transition → status-output flow is understandable.

